"}]}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "id": 10, "type": "RSLT"}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn8le16ob11re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "responses": [{"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Present an urban legend.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le16ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn8le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p>It has been one of the craziest weeks ever. I heard several amazing stories, but two stories stand out. The first one, involved that accident where the man was thrown from his car and where his broken body was found high atop the freeway sign.</p>\nStories have been written and movies have been made that don&rsquo;t even come close to being this bizarre. &nbsp;I have never heard of anything like that happening before and I probably never will hear about a story like that again. How did he get up there? There has to be an explanation. Right? Maybe."}, {"time": "31000", "image": "engenn8le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p>Another story, was about the remorseful robber. He robbed a bank, ran out with the money and came back five minutes later. He then waited for the police to come. Why did he go back to bank? I don&rsquo;t know.</p>\nThe point is, as a writer, I want to know. &nbsp;It is these amazing stories about insane coincidences, ridiculous experiences, and bizarre events that make life worth living. It is stories like these that feed my curiosity and make me want to learn more about everything."}, {"time": "60000", "image": "engenn8le16ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "So tell me your peculiar stories from a friend of the friend or an acquaintance that may be true or may be completely bogus because I have traveled around the world and I have had many experiences, but one of the best things in life is still sharing stories with friends. I will never tire of them and I can&rsquo;t wait for the next ones.<br/>"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1}, {"type": "static", "template_override": 1, "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: Hey Sam, have you ever dreamt about something bizarre? </br><span class=\"strong\">\nSam</span>: I have! The most peculiar dream I have had is about me living with cats. What about you? </br><span class=\"strong\">\nTom</span>: That's hilarious! Well, I have dreamt about living on Mars and having a restaurant for animals. <span class=\"strong\"></br>\nSam</span>: Really? Have you ever dreamt of falling from a really high place? </br><span class=\"strong\">\nTom</span>: I once dreamt about being on a high mountain but I was flying over it, so technically I didn't fall. "}], "id": 2}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Coincidences", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "There Must Be an Explanation", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the active voice when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject.<br/>You use the passive voice when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\">The car </span>(subject)<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">hit</span> the freeway sign</span> (object).<br/>Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\">The freeway sign </span>(subject)<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">was hit</span> by the car </span>(object).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It is not always necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be</span> verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Present passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "am/are/is + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were told</span> that story several times before.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Past passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "was/were + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>People <span class=\"strong\">were missed</span> by oncoming cars.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The man was thrown from his car.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "His broken body was found high atop the freeway sign. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Stories have been written.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Movies have been made.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience.<br/>When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I have learned English</span> = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English.<br/><span class=\"italic\">He has bought a painting</span> = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To emphasize the result of the action, use the simple form.<br/><br/></span><ul><li>Have you been out of the country yet?</li><li>I've traveled to Europe a couple of times.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It has been one of the craziest weeks ever.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I have never heard of anything like that happening before.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have traveled around the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have had many experiences.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in your blog about stories.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "remorseful", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling sad or guilty for having done something wrong", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Another story was about the remorseful robber.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "insane", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very irrational or crazy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is these amazing stories about insane coincidences and ridiculous experiences that I love.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "peculiar", "type": "name"}, {"content": "strange, often in an unpleasant way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So tell me your peculiar stories.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "friend of a friend", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone that you know; an acquaintance ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So tell me your peculiar stories from a friend of the friend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "acquaintance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone you know a little but is not a close friend", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So tell me your peculiar stories from a friend of the friend or an acquaintance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "can't wait", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used for saying someone is very excited about something happening ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I will never tire of them and I can't wait for the next ones.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Research an urban legend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make your presentation 3 to 5 minutes long.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask classmates to decide after if the urban legend is true or if it is false and give explanations as to why.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Brainstorm about the signs that tell us if an urban legend is true or not.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about past events a an urban legend. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss experiences people have had.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make presentations about urban legends.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use critical thinking.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}